      "writtenOn": "2020-12-02T16:58:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I agree, but here, as above, we may be constrained by what the TCPC does for us.\n\nCarrier mode has a timer, and there is an escape hatch for shared test mode. (We can exit \"if the tester makes a request that exceeds the capabilities of the UUT.)\n\nThe only specified way to get out of test data mode is to receive a Hard Reset. The GRL tester tends to use a disconnect, which also seems like a good time to get out of test mode.",
      "parentUuid": "7943a549_bf1c4ba9",
      "revId": "afd64b291b31b086d841487acbd0c44a287e0c81",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
